      <RemainingDuration>PT128H0M0S</RemainingDuration><RemainingWork>PT128H0M0S</RemainingWork>
      <ResumeValid>0</ResumeValid><Estimated>0</Estimated><ConstraintType>0</ConstraintType>
      <CalendarUID>-1</CalendarUID><FreeformDurationFormat>7</FreeformDurationFormat><EffortDriven>0</EffortDriven>
      <Notes>Three-server split: SQL-A hosts BizTalkMsgBoxDb (highest I/O, isolated for performance). SQL-B hosts BizTalkDTADb (tracking, isolated to prevent DTA archiving from impacting MsgBox). SQL-C hosts BizTalkMgmtDb, SSODB, BizTalkRuleEngineDb, BAMPrimaryImport, BAMArchive, BAMStarSchema, BAMAlertsApplication, BAMAlertsNSMain. Three parallel restore lanes during cutover produce the shortest maintenance window in the three-server model. SampleUpdateInfo.xml requires three separate server name entries. Logins must exist on all three instances.</Notes>
      <Hyperlink>BizTalk Server Database Overview</Hyperlink>
      <HyperlinkAddress>https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/biztalk/core/databases-in-biztalk-server</HyperlinkAddress>
    </Task>
