      <RemainingDuration>PT8H0M0S</RemainingDuration><RemainingWork>PT8H0M0S</RemainingWork>
      <ResumeValid>0</ResumeValid><Estimated>0</Estimated><ConstraintType>0</ConstraintType>
      <CalendarUID>-1</CalendarUID><FreeformDurationFormat>7</FreeformDurationFormat><EffortDriven>1</EffortDriven>
      <Notes>Maintenance window execution sequence: (1) Disable all receive locations and stop all BizTalk host instances. (2) Take final tail-log backups on source SQL. (3) Launch coordinator script — three restore lanes run in parallel: Lane-A restores BizTalkMsgBoxDb to SQL-A, Lane-B restores BizTalkDTADb to SQL-B, Lane-C restores Admin/BAM databases to SQL-C. (4) Coordinator blocks until all three lanes complete WITH RECOVERY. (5) Apply logins to all three servers. Deploy SQL Agent jobs to owning servers. (6) Update SampleUpdateInfo.xml (three entries) and run UpdateDatabase.vbs. (7) Start host instances, re-enable receive locations. (8) Process test messages. The three-way parallel restore compresses the maintenance window to approximately 8 hours because restore I/O is fully distributed.</Notes>
      <Hyperlink>How to Move the BizTalk Server Databases</Hyperlink>
      <HyperlinkAddress>https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/biztalk/core/how-to-move-the-biztalk-server-databases</HyperlinkAddress>
    </Task>
